# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/
**/target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock
**/Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb
.idea/
.run/
.env
.local/
/Docker/.erlang.cookie
/Doc/.*.drawio.bkp
/**/.DS_Store
src/.DS_Store
/*.profraw
/coverage/*.info
/cobertura.xml
/tarpaulin-report.html
.secrets
# `/scripts/` holds untracked personal helper scripts (e.g. `smoke-test.sh`).
# The `check_panic_policy.py` enforcement gate (issue #242) and its fixtures
# ARE tracked — Cargo.toml's `include` list has no `scripts/**` glob, so they
# never ship in the published crate either way.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/check_panic_policy.py
!/scripts/panic_policy_fixtures/
!/scripts/panic_policy_fixtures/*.rs
!/scripts/bench_compare.sh

# `scripts/bench_compare.sh` (issue #258) writes raw per-round JSON,
# system info and a summary into a fresh timestamped directory here on
# every run. Kept out of git entirely — it is scratch output, not
# source, and living outside `benches/` keeps it out of
# `Cargo.toml`'s `include = ["benches/**/*", ...]` (published crate
# tarball) regardless. A maintainer who wants to publish a comparison
# copies its `summary.md` into `BENCH.md` / `BENCHMARKS.md` by hand, the
# same way every existing comparison table in those files was produced.
/bench-results/

# Temporary files
tmp_reply.json

# Windsurf workflow files (never commit)
.windsurf/

# Internal documentation (never commit)
.internalDoc/
/.windsurfrules
.full_engine_diff.patch
smoke-results.json

# Local-only files: the contributor rules and review benchmark output.
rules/global_rules.md
target-review/
